{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_b855fcfbe58c2121a334c2513986a23a4d0238d9ce9feb84fe131738ae75a934", "title": "Mehmet Fuat Köprülü", "text": "Mehmet Fuat Köprülü (December 5, 1890 – June 28, 1966), also known as Köprülüzade Mehmed Fuad, was a highly influential Turcologist, Professor Ordinarius, Minister of Foreign Affairs and Deputy Prime Minister of the Republic of Turkey. A descendent of the illustrious Köprülü family, whose influence in shaping Ottoman history between 1656 and 1683 surpassed even that of the House of Osman, Fuat Köprülü was a key figure in the intersection of scholarship and politics in early 20th century Turkey. As a historian and public intellectual, his books, articles, essays and poems forged a “canon of Turkish culture and national identity” that provided the newly formed Republic of Turkey with scholarly sources of Turkishness.", "score": 23.5567}, {"id": "hp_doc_b0c3fbc93297595d1aa916275c9a6da610475f1a6fd8f316b8921eec1b025347", "title": "Fuat Bulca", "text": "Ahmet Fuat Bulca (1881 – September 14, 1962) was an officer of the Ottoman Army and Turkish Army and a Turkish politician. He was the one of the closest friend of Mustafa Kemal (Atatürk), as well as his classmate at the Monastir Military High School.", "score": 23.0298}, {"id": "hp_doc_a6723c52cd0e1711c85323139008478c929cf2786896de4943722b8d9c9d0a96", "title": "Bulca, Sinanpaşa", "text": "Bulca is a village in the District of Sinanpaşa, Afyonkarahisar Province, Turkey.", "score": 22.9264}], "remaining_searches": 2}
